# Business Analysis - IELTS Fighter CRM Project

## 1. Situation Before CRM Deployment

Before the CRM system, IELTS Fighter's enrollment and student care processes mainly relied on manual and fragmented tools:

- **Scattered lead management**: Lead information was stored in many places (Excel, Google Sheets, website forms, Zalo, Facebook, Email…).
- **Manual tracking**: Call schedules, entrance test appointments, and follow-ups were recorded separately and easy to miss.
- **Inconsistent consultation process**: Each advisor followed their own method, causing uneven customer experience.
- **Fragmented student care**: Class schedules, attendance, make-up lessons, and student feedback were managed by different departments (Customer Service, Academic Affairs, Training).
- **Marketing lacked measurement**: It was difficult to assess the effectiveness of advertising channels (CPL, Conversion Rate).
- **Slow and manual reporting**: Management lacked real-time reports on recruitment performance and student status.

## 2. Main Issues

- Lead loss due to untimely follow-up and unclear responsibility.
- Low lead conversion rate due to unstructured follow-up.
- Uneven service quality among advisors.
- Difficulty creating personalized learning plans because of missing student history.
- Inability to accurately evaluate employee performance.
- Marketing costs wasted due to inability to measure channel effectiveness.

## 3. CRM Deployment Objectives

### General objective
Build a centralized CRM system, standardize the enrollment process, and improve student care quality at IELTS Fighter.

### Specific objectives
- Centralize lead and student data.
- Standardize the process from Marketing → Consultation → Enrollment → Customer Service.
- Automate follow-up and reminders.
- Provide real-time reports to support management.
- Integrate website lead forms and advertising channels.

## 4. Main Functional Requirements

- **Lead & Pipeline Management**: Track progress from Lead → Test → Consultation → Registration.
- **Course & Class Management**: Course catalog, class management, schedule management.
- **Tuition Management**: Create invoices, track payments, manage receivables.
- **Progress & Customer Care Management**: Student profiles, schedules, feedback, periodic care.
- **Reporting**: Sales performance, lead quality, revenue, dropout rate.
- **Integration & Automation**: Website lead forms, API, automatic email/SMS sending.

